      "content": "You would likely encounter the most resistance when attempting to frame territorial claims in terms of moral duty or historical reverence, as modern power politics is overwhelmingly codified by international law and military capability. To bridge this gap, instead of invoking \"oaths,\" frame ancestral duty as \"deep, non-negotiable vested interest\"—a concept that translates respect for heritage into a strategic bargaining chip. This reframing allows the concept to be discussed in the language of national security rather than abstract spiritual commitment.",
